  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Then the number of elements in the relation&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>divides</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>divides</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is",
